        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Picture it. You're running late, you slide the key in, twist, and the thing just sits there. Car key won't turn in the ignition. Ugh. Before you start sweating, know this: it's almost always something small. The steering wheel lock gets the blame most days. Now and then it's a tired key, a shifter that isn't quite in Park, or a little gunk in the keyway. We'll check them one by one.
        </p>

