          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-12 mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 not-prose">

          <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              Why won't my car key turn in the ignition?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Nine times in ten, the steering wheel lock. Wiggle the wheel gently while you turn the key. If that doesn't do it, make sure the car is fully in Park, then look the key over for wear or a bend.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              How do I get a key out of the ignition when it is stuck?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">First, confirm the car is fully in Park, and press the brake if your model wants it. Wiggle the wheel, then try again. Don't yank on it. Still won't come out? A locksmith can free it without hurting the cylinder.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              Can a worn key stop the ignition from turning?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">It can, yes. Once the ridges wear down, the pins in the cylinder stop lining up the way they should. Spare turns smoothly? Then the original is the worn one.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
            <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
              Is it safe to use WD-40 in a car ignition?
              <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
            </summary>
